REVISE

REASONS
1. [High] `render_html` inserts design-token values directly into inline CSS without escaping, so `app_set_design` can inject into `<style>` and break out into executable content. See [`render_html`](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/core/src/disco/core/appkit/models.py). This violates the stated “html-escaped” safety expectation for rendering.
2. [Medium] `app_snapshot_version` default label is not a sequence despite the docstring intent; it uses `len(spec.sections)` plus `hash(spec.model_dump_json())` and Python’s randomized hash makes names unstable across runs plus collision-prone due modulo. See [`AppSnapshotVersionTool`](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/tools/src/disco/tools/builtin/appkit.py). This is a regression risk for deterministic snapshot history and can overwrite/reuse labels unintentionally.
3. [Medium] `AppCreateTool` accepts section lists with duplicate `id`s because there is no uniqueness validation in `AppSpec`/`create`. Duplicate ids make `section_id` lookups ambiguous for later targeted edits (`app_update_content`, reorder/remove), reducing correctness of semantic operations. See [`AppCreateTool.run`](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/tools/src/disco/tools/builtin/appkit.py) and [`AppSpec`](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/core/src/disco/core/appkit/models.py).
